// Package api is the Win32 functions, types and constants
// `sngl:platform/win32` calls, as `#[cnative]` declarations a program may call
// too.
//
// `api.sngl` is generated by `go tool win32gen` from win32json, a JSON
// rendering of Microsoft's win32metadata, at a pinned commit, and each type is
// spelled as MinGW's headers spell it. A handle (`HWND`, `HDC`) is an opaque
// struct, a typedef of an integer (`UINT`, `WPARAM`) an alias of `int` that
// crosses as that typedef, a struct of such fields (`RECT`) a C struct, and a
// string a function reads as UTF-16 a `c.utf16`. A function is named without
// its `W` where Win32 also has an `A` one. What C interop cannot cross -- a
// buffer, a pointer to a struct the callee reads, a function declared only as
// a macro on one architecture -- is listed at the end of `api.sngl` and called
// from the platform's C runtime instead.
